use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../../behaviors/Announcement import Announcement
from ../Button import Button

export ui-component CopyButton:
    description:
        A copy button copies a piece of text to the clipboard when pressed,
        such as a link, an access key or a code snippet, and briefly shows
        that it worked.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    behaviors:
        - @{Announcement}

    value:
        The component gives the text to copy, and can change it at any time.
        It is often shown next to the button, but doesn't have to be. Pressing
        the button copies the whole text, as it is at that moment.

    confirmation:
        After copying, the button changes for a short while to show it worked,
        such as a tick in place of its icon, or "Copied" in place of its label.
        It then goes back to how it was. Pressing it again during that time
        copies again and starts the time over. How long it lasts is up to the
        component.

    announcing:
        Assistive tools are told the text was copied, without focus moving.
        The button's name stays the same while it shows the confirmation.

    failure:
        Copying can fail, for example if the platform doesn't allow it. The
        button then doesn't show that it worked. The user is told it didn't
        work, and the component is told too.

    nonGoals:
        - Text only. Whether pictures or formatted content can be copied is up
            to the chosen library and platform
        - No pasting or reading from the clipboard
